      "content": "That is a very astute point regarding historical anachronism. You raise a valid argument that judging ancient political maneuvering by modern moral standards is perhaps unfair. In the hyper-competitive, zero-sum political landscape of classical warfare, calculated opportunism was often a survival mechanism. Therefore, framing him as a master strategist navigating a treacherous game offers a historically more nuanced view than simply labeling him immoral.",
      "source": "target",
